meta {
  name: Get Agency Profile
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/agency/profile
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ownerAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("reports the agency name, an IANA time zone and a whole end-of-day hour", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.agencyName).to.be.a("string").and.not.be.empty;
    expect(body.timezone).to.match(/^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_+-]*(\/[A-Za-z0-9_+-]+)*$/);
    expect(Number.isInteger(body.endOfDayHour)).to.equal(true);
    expect(body.endOfDayHour).to.be.within(0, 23);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /agency/profile — the agency's working day (PAC-141, PAC-149)

  The owner-editable facts about the agency itself: the IANA zone it keeps its
  working day in, and the hour on that clock after which everyone is set Away.

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`) — the agency's identity is not a
    product module that can be switched off.
  - **Permission:** `agency:settings:read` — its own pair since PAC-149.
    PAC-141 reused `agency:branding:read` for the zone alone; with the
    end-of-day hour beside it the page sets the whole office Away each night,
    and an owner delegating "branding" must not hand that over unknowingly.
    By default only the Agency Owner holds it; existing owners received it
    from the `agency_settings_permission_grant` migration.
  - **Data scope:** none — the caller's own agency, from the token.

  ## What the zone drives
  - Every dashboard date window — `today`, `week`, `mtd`, the Owner view's
    presets, the Manager view's business-day aging, the leaderboard's default
    month — is cut on this calendar (`AccessContext.timeZone`, resolved once per
    request).
  - The clock the end-of-day Away sweep reads (`Set My Availability`).
  - The calendar day an app-written quote recap is filed on.

  ## What the hour drives
  - The end-of-day Away sweep and nothing else: from `endOfDayHour:00` on the
    agency's clock, every active user of the agency is set `away`, once per
    local date. A whole hour, `0`–`23` (`20` = 8 PM), because the sweep ticks
    every thirty minutes.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  { "agencyName": "Smith Family Agency", "timezone": "America/Chicago", "endOfDayHour": 20 }
  ```

  Defaults to `America/Chicago` (US Central) and `20` (8 PM) for every agency
  that has never set them; the Super Admin onboarding wizard pre-selects the
  same zone.

  ## Errors
  - `403` — caller lacks `agency:settings:read`.
}
